On 2 Oct 1993 13:17:15 +0200, walker@mits.mdata.fi (Jukka Lahtinen) said:

> scythe@stein3.u.washington.edu (The Grim Reaper) writes:

>>and dropped the corpse.  However, since it doesn't check to see your 
>>weight status until the next turn, you still had to wait through those
>>pauses from being overloaded!  R.I.P.

> So, there would be an easy (at least I think it'd be easy, however I don't
> have the source..) solution:
> The game should check your weight and carrying capacity AFTER your move
> instead of checking it before you move.

Actually, I think it would have to check at both times.  Otherwise,
something could happen to change your carried weight after some monsters
had hit you but before your next move.  E.g. a blast of fire hits you and
burns some spellbooks.  The change in weight needs to be noted before
you move; e.g. if you were previously overtaxed and couldn't move, but
now could move, or vice versa, this would need to be noticed before
you move.

